- grove_install
- shrine_types
- bond

' Networked names: the generic substrate for one world observing another's
' published names.  Activation instantiates the Grove template at /<self>/net
' and mounts the stale overlay as a cell over the whole names subtree:
' /net/names/<publisher>/<name>/current is written by the shrine-mesa sidecar
' (the acquired, source-attributed revision), /seen beside it by whoever
' judged against that revision, and /x/net/stale lists the names whose
' acquired revision has moved past the one that was judged.  The cell is
' written here rather than seeded in Grove because a Grove tack is y-care
' only and the names subtree is three deep.
+ net_mount
  + failure
    : reason=iota
  + install
    \ state=namespace
    ^ either[pail namespace]
    = source=path [state.self 'gov 'net]
    ?> (./some version) state.case(.x source)
      | ./err (pails/t "Missing net template")
    = installed=either[pail namespace]
        ? (grove_install/instantiate source version [state.self 'net] state)
         > (./ok next) (./ok next)
         > (./err why) (./err (net_mount/failure why))
    < next installed
    = overlay (myth/sing bond/weft (safe 1 .x [state.self 'gov 'net 'stale]))
      overlay overlay.put(bond/tack (safe 0 .z [state.self 'net 'names]))
    ? (grove_install/change [state.self 'net 'stale] (writ/make overlay) next)
     > (./ok next) (./ok next)
     > (./err why) (./err (net_mount/failure why))
